        "original_id": "bd5110dc-2f06-5948-9fdb-9fcc173a1c2a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Kyosuke Himuro, Boy George, Yukinojo Mori, Dominic J. Hawken, George Alan O'Dowd\n- Organizations: Boøwy\n- Songs: \"Do You Really Want to Hurt Me\", \"Time (Clock of the Heart)\", \"Karma Chameleon\"\n- Topics: music careers, songwriting, anime theme songs\n\nFacts:\n- Kyosuke Himuro was born on October 7, 1960, in Takasaki, Gunma, Japan.\n- Kyosuke Himuro is a Japanese singer-songwriter and musician.\n- Boy George, born George Alan O'Dowd, was born on 14 June 1961.\n- Boy George is an English singer, songwriter, DJ, fashion designer, and photographer.\n- Dominic J. Hawken was born in 1967.\n- Kyosuke Himuro was the lead vocalist of the rock band Boøwy from 1981 to 1988.\n- During the 1980s, Boy George's band recorded global hit songs including \"Do You Really Want to Hurt Me\", \"Time (Clock of the Heart)\", and \"Karma Chameleon\".\n- Boy George is known for his soulful voice and androgynous appearance.\n- Dominic J. Hawken was a keyboard player and session musician in the 1990s and originally played with Boy George and Marilyn.\n- Yukinojo Mori has written over 2,000 songs for artists including Kyosuke Himuro, Takuro Yoshida, and Junichi Inagaki.\n- Yukinojo Mori has also written theme songs for anime series including \"Dragon Ball Z\".",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
